WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.140
What message would you
guys like the gatekeepers

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.280
of Hollywood, studio heads,
producers, the writers,

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:11.430
the casting directors,
what message would you

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.320
like them to know?

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:23.520
I think I would love to let
them know that they shouldn't

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.770
get too overwhelmed right now.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.230
I think we're in a really
big process of change.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.970
And there are a
lot of people who

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.030
are wanting to share their
stories and their experiences.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.870
And I think that there are so
many more people we should be

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.150
welcoming into this industry.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.460
I would love for them
to be more open-minded

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:44.600
about closed captioning,
not only for people

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.000
who speak English,
but for those who

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.800
are deaf and hard
of hearing, as well

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.350
as those who speak other
languages in other countries.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:56.090
I know that here we primarily
look at everything with a lens

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.280
that we're Americans,
but I think

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.390
that we have so
much rich knowledge,

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.470
and there's media out
there that we could share.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.930
I think we need to be
doing more listening.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:11.120
We need to be more
compassionate.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.370
And that's what I would
like them to know.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:24.970
I am going to say about the
writers, writer and directors,

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:33.400
I would say they
are so very awesome,

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:44.720
awesome and great and plus,
the producers have been working

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.940
very hard and are focused
and doing all the camera,

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.700
then go from --

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:56.570
I would say both ways
and do that and do this.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:02.210
So they have been doing a
pretty, pretty good job.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:03.050
That's great.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:06.920
I would say to writers, put in
characters with disabilities.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.759
Directors, talk to consultants
to help you with this stuff.

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:14.786
And then when casting,
cast disabled people.

00:02:14.786 --> 00:02:18.050
It used to be that
non-disabled people loved

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.580
to play disabled people.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.520
But now, let disabled
people play themselves.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.140
So that's what I would
love Hollywood to do.

